---
description: Keep tests focused. Don't duplicate cases that exercise the same path.
globs: '**/*.test.ts,**/*.test.tsx'
alwaysApply: true
---

Don't duplicate the same case for every union variant when the code path is
shared. One representative value is enough unless the type changes behavior.

```ts
// Avoid — add/delete behave the same for automatic and manual boxes
it('deletes an automatic box', ...);
it('deletes a manual box', ...);

// Prefer — one variant covers the shared lookup
it('deletes a box by page, type, and coordinates', ...);
```

Don't write a test whose only job is to prove an npm library works. Trust
croner, yargs, and the like.

Don't assert the same fact two ways. If `findAll` by IDs already shows the
row is gone, do not also `.reload()` that instance. Add a second check only
when it is a different fact, such as Spaces objects vs database rows.

Comment what each assertion group is checking, next to those expects:

```ts
// Expect the idle rows to be gone; only the fresh ID should come back.
expect(remaining.map((row) => row.id)).toEqual([fresh.id]);

// Expect the idle PDF and page images to be gone from Spaces.
await expect(getRedactionFile(stale.key)).rejects.toMatchObject({
  name: 'NotFound',
});
```
